ises":[{"id":940,"name":"Bench press","description":"The bench press is a popular barbell exercise that builds strength and muscle in the chest, triceps, and shoulders. It is a popular way to measure overall upper-body strength, and is contested in the sport of powerlifting. When many people think of lifting, the bench press is often the first exercise that comes to mind. It can be performed for low reps for strength, higher reps for muscle, or for higher reps to build or measure strength endurance, like in the 225-pound bench press rep test in the NFL combine.","type":"Strength","body_part":"Chest","equipment":"Barbell","level":"Intermediate","name_fr":"Développé couché","display_name":"Bench press","pivot":{"custom_workout_id":1,"gym_exercise_id":940,"sets":4,"reps":8,"duration":null,"rest":120}},{"id":1107,"name":"Incline Dumbbell Flyes","description":"The incline dumbbell chest fly is an upper body isolation exercise targeting the upper chest and is typically used with aesthetic goals in mind. It will require less weight than an incline press, which makes it a great hypertrophy exercise with high reps.","type":"Strength","body_part":"Chest","equipment":"Dumbbell","level":"Intermediate","name_fr":"Écartés avec haltères sur banc incliné","display_name":"Incline Dumbbell Flyes","pivot":{"custom_workout_id":1,"gym_exercise_id":1107,"sets":3,"reps":12,"duration":null,"rest":90}},{"id":2635,"name":"MetaBurn Dumbbell Overhead Press","description":"","type":"Strength","body_part":"Shoulders","equipment":"Dumbbell","level":"Intermediate","name_fr":"Développé couché avec haltères MetaBurn","display_name":"MetaBurn Dumbbell Overhead Press","pivot":{"custom_workout_id":1,"gym_exercise_id":2635,"sets":3,"reps":10,"duration":null,"rest":90}},{"id":2539,"name":"Side Lateral Raise","description":"The dumbbell lateral raise is an upper body isolation exercise for building shoulder strength and muscle. It's a staple strength training move and is a great option for accessory work on upper body training days. This exercise particularly focuses on the lateral or medial head of the deltoid, making them appear wider and more developed.","type":"Strength","body_part":"Shoulders","equipment":"Dumbbell","level":"Intermediate","name_fr":"Élévation latérale","display_name":"Side Lateral Raise","pivot":{"custom_workout_id":1,"gym_exercise_id":2539,"sets":3,"reps":15,"duration":null,"rest":60}},{"id":2848,"name":"Cable rope push-down","description":"The cable rope push-down is a popular exercise targeting the triceps muscles. It's easy to learn and perform, making it a favorite for everyone from beginners to advanced lifters. It is usually performed for moderate to high reps, such as 8-12 reps or more per set, as part of an upper-body or arm-focused workout.","type":"Strength","body_part":"Triceps","equipment":"Cable","level":"Intermediate","name_fr":"Poussée vers le bas avec un câble","display_name":"Cable rope push-down","pivot":{"custom_workout_id":1,"gym_exercise_id":2848,"sets":3,"reps":12,"duration":null,"rest":60}}]},{"id":2,"user_id":1,"name":"Pull Day","description":"Back and biceps","gym_exercises":[{"id":1503,"name":"Pull-up","description":"The pull-up is a multijoint bodyweight exercise that builds strength and muscle in the upper back, biceps, and core. It is often used as a measurement tool in military or tactical fitness tests, and is an excellent gauge of \"relative strength\" which is strength in relation to body weight.","type":"Strength","body_part":"Lats","equipment":"Body Only","level":"Beginner","name_fr":"Traction","display_name":"Pull-up","pivot":{"custom_workout_id":2,"gym_exercise_id":1503,"sets":4,"reps":8,"duration":null,"rest":120}},{"id":1637,"name":"Bent Over Barbell Row","description":"The barbell bent-over row is a compound exercise used to build strength and size in both the lower and upper back. It targets nearly all of the muscles in the back, but particularly the lats, rhomboids, and lower back. It is commonly utilized as an accessory movement for the deadlift in powerlifting, but is also popular in strength and muscle-focused upper-body workouts.","type":"Strength","body_part":"Middle Back","equipment":"Barbell","level":"Intermediate","name_fr":"Rameur penché avec haltère long","display_name":"Bent Over Barbell Row","pivot":{"custom_workout_id":2,"gym_exercise_id":1637,"sets":4,"reps":10,"duration":null,"rest":90}},{"id":1695,"name":"Seated Cable Rows","description":"The cable seated row is a popular exercise to train the muscles of the upper back, including the lats (latissimus dorsi), traps, rhomboids, and rear deltoids, using a cable stack. It also targets the biceps to a lesser degree. The cable row can work well in a variety of rep-ranges, but is most popular in muscle-building workouts or as an accessory movement for strength workouts.","type":"Strength","body_part":"Middle Back","equipment":"Cable","level":"Intermediate","name_fr":"Rameur à câble en position assise","display_name":"Seated Cable Rows","pivot":{"custom_workout_id":2,"gym_exercise_id":1695,"sets":3,"reps":12,"duration":null,"rest":90}},{"id":2679,"name":"Standing face pull","description":"The standing face pull is an isolation exercise primarily targeting the rear deltoids, traps, and upper back. It is most often performed with a rope attachment.","type":"Strength","body_part":"Shoulders","equipment":"Cable","level":"Intermediate","name_fr":"Traction frontale debout","display_name":"Standing face pull","pivot":{"custom_workout_id":2,"gym_exercise_id":2679,"sets":3,"reps":15,"duration":null,"rest":60}},{"id":735,"name":"Dumbbell Bicep Curl","description":"The dumbbell biceps curl is a single-joint exercise for building bigger and stronger biceps. Popular among gym goers of all experience levels, this move can be done seated or standing. It is generally performed for moderate to high reps, such as 8-12 reps or higher, as part of the arm-focused portion of a workout.","type":"Strength","body_part":"Biceps","equipment":"Dumbbell","level":"Intermediate","name_fr":"Curl des biceps avec haltères","display_name":"Dumbbell Bicep Curl","pivot":{"custom_workout_id":2,"gym_exercise_id":735,"sets":3,"reps":12,"duration":null,"rest":60}}]},{"id":3,"user_id":1,"name":"Leg Day","description":"Quads, hamstrings, glutes and calves","gym_exercises":[{"id":1817,"name":"Barbell back squat","description":"The barbell back squat is a popular compound movement that emphasizes building the lower-body muscle groups and overall strength. It's the classic way to start a leg day, and is a worthy centerpiece to a lower-body training program. The squat is a competitive lift in the sport of powerlifting, but is also a classic measurement of lower-body strength. With the barbell racked on the traps or upper back, the emphasis is placed on the posterior chain but the entire body gets worked. The back squat can be trained in everything from heavy singles to sets of 20 reps or higher.","type":"Strength","body_part":"Quadriceps","equipment":"Barbell","level":"Intermediate","name_fr":"Squat arrière avec haltères","display_name":"Barbell back squat","pivot":{"custom_workout_id":3,"gym_exercise_id":1817,"sets":4,"reps":8,"duration":null,"rest":150}},{"id":1302,"name":"Romanian Deadlift","description":"The barbell stiff-legged deadlift targets the hamstrings, glutes, lower and upper back, as well as the core. It is a popular accessory movement for the deadlift, but also a muscle-building hamstring movement.","type":"Strength","body_part":"Hamstrings","equipment":"Barbell","level":"Intermediate","name_fr":"Soulevé de terre roumain","display_name":"Romanian Deadlift","pivot":{"custom_workout_id":3,"gym_exercise_id":1302,"sets":3,"reps":10,"duration":null,"rest":120}},{"id":2061,"name":"Leg Press","description":"The leg press is a machine exercise targeting the quadriceps. It’s favorite among lifters who prefer the seated position to standing with a load on the spine.","type":"Strength","body_part":"Quadriceps","equipment":"Machine","level":"Intermediate","name_fr":"Presse à jambes","display_name":"Leg Press","pivot":{"custom_workout_id":3,"gym_exercise_id":2061,"sets":3,"reps":12,"duration":null,"rest":90}},{"id":1262,"name":"Walking lunge","description":"The walking lunge is a lower-body exercise that targets the glutes, quads, and hamstrings while challenging stability and balance. It can be performed for reps, time, or distance in the lower-body portion of any workout.","type":"Strength","body_part":"Glutes","equipment":"Body Only","level":"Intermediate","name_fr":"Fente en marchant","display_name":"Walking lunge","pivot":{"custom_workout_id":3,"gym_exercise_id":1262,"sets":3,"reps":12,"duration":null,"rest":90}},{"id":908,"name":"Standing Calf Raise","description":"The standing calf raise is a popular movement to target the calf muscles of the lower leg, and in particular the gastrocnemius muscles. When unweighted, it is usually performed for high reps or for time.","type":"Strength","body_part":"Calves","equipment":"Body Only","level":"Intermediate","name_fr":"Extension des mollets debout","display_name":"Standing Calf Raise","pivot":{"custom_workout_id":3,"gym_exercise_id":908,"sets":4,"reps":15,"duration":null,"rest":60}}]},{"id":4,"user_id":1,"name":"Full Body & Core","description":"A lighter full-body session to end the week","gym_exercises":[{"id":1918,"name":"Dumbbell Walking Lunge","description":"The dumbbell walking lunge tests your ability to maintain balance while challenging the quads, glutes, and hamstrings as well as core muscles.","type":"Strength","body_part":"Quadriceps","equipment":"Dumbbell","level":"Intermediate","name_fr":"Fente avant avec haltères","display_name":"Dumbbell Walking Lunge","pivot":{"custom_workout_id":4,"gym_exercise_id":1918,"sets":3,"reps":12,"duration":null,"rest":90}},{"id":1474,"name":"Full Range-Of-Motion Lat Pulldown","description":"","type":"Strength","body_part":"Lats","equipment":"Cable","level":"Beginner","name_fr":"T