exercise for building bigger and stronger biceps. Popular among gym goers of all experience levels, this move can be done seated or standing. It is generally performed for moderate to high reps, such as 8-12 reps or higher, as part of the arm-focused portion of a workout.","type":"Strength","body_part":"Biceps","equipment":"Dumbbell","level":"Intermediate","name_fr":"Curl des biceps avec haltères","display_name":"Curl des biceps avec haltères","pivot":{"custom_workout_id":2,"gym_exercise_id":735,"sets":3,"reps":12,"duration":null,"rest":60}}]},{"id":3,"user_id":1,"name":"Séance jambes","description":"Quadriceps, ischios, fessiers et mollets","gym_exercises":[{"id":1817,"name":"Barbell back squat","description":"The barbell back squat is a popular compound movement that emphasizes building the lower-body muscle groups and overall strength. It's the classic way to start a leg day, and is a worthy centerpiece to a lower-body training program. The squat is a competitive lift in the sport of powerlifting, but is also a classic measurement of lower-body strength. With the barbell racked on the traps or upper back, the emphasis is placed on the posterior chain but the entire body gets worked. The back squat can be trained in everything from heavy singles to sets of 20 reps or higher.","type":"Strength","body_part":"Quadriceps","equipment":"Barbell","level":"Intermediate","name_fr":"Squat arrière avec haltères","display_name":"Squat arrière avec haltères","pivot":{"custom_workout_id":3,"gym_exercise_id":1817,"sets":4,"reps":8,"duration":null,"rest":150}},{"id":1302,"name":"Romanian Deadlift","description":"The barbell stiff-legged deadlift targets the hamstrings, glutes, lower and upper back, as well as the core. It is a popular accessory movement for the deadlift, but also a muscle-building hamstring movement.","type":"Strength","body_part":"Hamstrings","equipment":"Barbell","level":"Intermediate","name_fr":"Soulevé de terre roumain","display_name":"Soulevé de terre roumai